title: Elder
---
<<if has_flag("quest_started")>>
    Elder: The Crest's shards flew east, toward Whisperwood.
    Elder: Rest at the campfire before you set out. Be careful, child.
<<else>>
    Elder: Kael... last night the Ashen Crest cracked. You saw how bad it was.
    Elder: That sacred ember protects this village. Without its shards, the Ashblight will keep spreading.
    Kael: I'll find them. Where did the shards go?
    Elder: East, through Whisperwood. Perhaps as far as the old Emberline mine.
    Lira: Then I'm coming too. Don't argue, Kael. Who else is going to patch you up?
    Kael: ...Fine. But stay close to me.
    Elder: Take these. May the ember watch over you both.
    <<flag quest_started>>
    <<give herbal 3>>
<<endif>>
===
title: Merchant
---
Merchant: Welcome! My shop hasn't reopened since the Crest cracked.
Merchant: If you're heading into the woods, find me some Ember Herbs. I'll pay you well.
===
title: Child
---
Child: Kael! The fire's gone dim, hasn't it? I'm scared of the monsters in the woods...
Lira: Don't worry. We'll make it burn bright again.
===
title: Guard
---
<<if has_flag("quest_started")>>
    Guard: So the Elder sent you. The beasts in Whisperwood are getting worse. Look after Lira.
<<else>>
    Guard: The east gate has been shut since last night. Speak with the Elder by the shrine first.
<<endif>>
===
title: Guard_Blocked
---
Guard: Hold on, Kael. The Elder wants a word before you go anywhere.
===
title: Sign_Whisperwood
---
Sign: → Whisperwood. Beware of wild beasts.
===
title: Shrine
---
The Ashen Crest's ember flickers weakly. A long crack splits its surface.
Lira: Strange... my chest feels warm whenever I stand near it.
===
title: Campfire
---
The campfire burns warm.
-> Rest and save
    <<rest>>
    The party is fully restored.
    <<save_menu>>
-> Just rest
    <<rest>>
    The party is fully restored.
-> Leave
===
